<article class="env-example" id="0GG5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GG5">Example <span data-tag="0GG5">86.3.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a proper morphism of Noetherian algebraic spaces over $S$, $L \in D^-_{\textit{Coh}}(X)$ and $K \in D^+_{\mathit{QCoh}}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$. Then the map $Rf_*R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ X}(L, a(K)) \to R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ Y}(Rf_*L, K)$ is an isomorphism. Namely, the complexes $L$ and $Rf_*L$ are pseudo-coherent by Derived Categories of Spaces, Lemmas <a href="/tag/08IK" data-tag="08IK">75.13.7</a> and <a href="/tag/08GK" data-tag="08GK">75.8.1</a> and the discussion in Remark <a href="/tag/0GG4" data-tag="0GG4">86.3.5</a> applies. </p>
</article>